{"G1111":{"id":"G1111","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1111","disambiguated_id":"G1111 =","unique_id":"G1111","headword":"γογγύζω","transliteration":"gonguzō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to murmur","definition_en":"γογγύζω, \n [in LXX chiefly for לוּן ;] \nto mutter, murmur: 1Co.10:10; before κατά, Mat.20:11; πρός, Luk.5:30; περί, Jhn.6:41, 61; μετ᾽ ἀλλήλων, Jhn.6:43; with accusative, before περί, Jhn.7:32 (cf. δια-γογγύζω).†\n (AS)","source_line":1242}],"occurrence_count":8,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"murmuravam","count":2},{"gloss":"murmuraram","count":2},{"gloss":"murmureis","count":2},{"gloss":"seus","count":1},{"gloss":"murmurava","count":1}]},"G1164":{"id":"G1164","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1164","disambiguated_id":"G1164 =","unique_id":"G1164","headword":"δεῖγμα","transliteration":"deigma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"example","definition_en":"δεῖγμα, -τος, τό \n (δείκνυμι); \n __1. (cl.) a thing shown, a specimen. \n __2. = cl. παράδ- (cf. ὑπόδ-, 2Pe.2:6), an example (a warning): Ju 7.† \n (AS)","source_line":1296}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"punição","count":1}]},"G1371":{"id":"G1371","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1371","disambiguated_id":"G1371 =","unique_id":"G1371","headword":"διχοτομέω","transliteration":"dichotomeō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to cut in two","definition_en":"διχοτομέω, -ῶ\n (διχοτόμος, δίχα, τέμνω), [in LXX: Exo.29:17 (נָתַח pi.) ;] \nto cut in two, cut asunder: perh. metaphorically of severe scourging (but see Meyer on Mt, l.with, and cf. 1Ki.15:33, 2Ki.12:31, Heb.11:37), Mat.24:51, Luk.12:46.†\n (AS)","source_line":1503}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"despedaçará-porá","count":1},{"gloss":"partido","count":1}]},"G1373":{"id":"G1373","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1373","disambiguated_id":"G1373 =","unique_id":"G1373","headword":"δίψος","transliteration":"dipsos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"thirst","definition_en":"δίψος, -εος (-ους), τό \n (late form of δίψα), [in LXX chiefly for and cognates ;] \nthirst: 2Co.11:27.†\n (AS)","source_line":1505}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sede","count":1}]},"G1785":{"id":"G1785","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1785","disambiguated_id":"G1785 =","unique_id":"G1785","headword":"ἐντολή","transliteration":"entolē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"commandment","definition_en":"ἐντολή, -ῆς, ἡ\n (ἐντέλλω, which see), [in LXX chiefly for מִצְוָה; in pl. frequently in Pss for פִּקּוּד ;] \n__1. generally, a charge, injunction, order, command: Luk.15:29, Jhn.10:18 11:57 12:49-50 14:31, Act.17:15, Col.4:10; ἐ. σαρκίνη, Heb.7:16, 18 \n __2. Esp. of religious precepts and commandments; \n __(a) of God's commandments: in OT, Mat.15:3 22:36, 38 22:40 Mk 7:8-9; Mrk.10:5, 19 12:28, 31 Eph.2:15, Heb.9:19; esp. of the decalogue, Mat.5:19 19:17, Mrk.10:19, Luk.18:20 23:56, Rom.7:8-13 13:9, Eph.6:2; of God's command­ments in general, Luk.1:6, 1Co.7:19, 1Jn.2:3-8 Jn 3:22-24 Jn 4:21 Jn 5:2-3, Rev.12:17 14:12; collectively, ἡ ἐ. (cf. τ. ἔργον τ. θεοῦ, Jhn.6:29), 1Ti.6:14, 2Pe.2:21 3:2; \n __(b) of things commanded Christ by the Father: Jhn.12:49-50 14:31 15:10; \n __(with) of the precepts of Christ: Jhn.13:34 14:15, 21 15:10, 12, 1Co.14:37. \n __3. Phrases: before ἵνα, Jhn.13:34 15:12, 1Jn.3:23 Jn 4:21, 2Jn.6; ἐντολὴν (ὰς) παραβαίνειν, Mat.15:3; ἀκυροῦν, Mat.15:6 Rec.; τηρεῖν, Mat.19:17 Jhn.15:10, al.; ποιεῖν, 1Jn.5:2; διδόναι, Jhn.11:57; λαμβάνειν, Jhn.10:18, 2Jn.4; ἔχειν, Jhn.14:21, Heb.7:5; ἐ. καὶ δικαιώματα, Luk.1:6; ἐντολαὶ ἀνθρώπων (of Jewish tradition), Tit.1:14; i. καινή, Jhn.13:34, 1Jn.2:7, 2Jn.5.†\n (AS)","source_line":1926}],"occurrence_count":66,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mandamento","count":37},{"gloss":"mandamentos","count":22},{"gloss":"ordem","count":4},{"gloss":"guardardes","count":1},{"gloss":"ordens","count":1},{"gloss":"ele","count":1}]},"G2216":{"id":"G2216","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2216","disambiguated_id":"G2216G =","unique_id":"G2216G","headword":"Ζοροβάβελ","transliteration":"Zorobabel","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Zerubbabel","definition_en":"Ζοροβάβελ (FlJ, Ζοροβάβηλος, -ου), ὁ indecl. (Heb. זְרֻבָּבֶל), \n Zerubbabel (1Ch.3:19, al.): Mat.1:12-13 Luk.3:27.†\n (AS)","source_line":2360},{"source_id":"G2216","disambiguated_id":"G2216H = the Greek of","unique_id":"H2216","headword":"Ζοροβάβελ","transliteration":"Zorobabel","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Zerubbabel","definition_en":"Ζοροβάβελ (FlJ, Ζοροβάβηλος, -ου), ὁ indecl. (Heb. זְרֻבָּבֶל), \n Zerubbabel (1Ch.3:19, al.): Mat.1:12-13 Luk.3:27.†\n (AS)","source_line":2361}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Zorobabel","count":3}]},"G2235":{"id":"G2235","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2235","disambiguated_id":"G2235 =","unique_id":"G2235","headword":"ἤδη","transliteration":"ēdē","lexical_morphology":"G:ADV","gloss_en":"already","definition_en":"ἤδη \n adv., \nin NT, always of time; now, already: Mat.3:10, Mrk.4:37, Luk.7:6, Jhn.4:36, al.; νῦν . . . ἤ., now already, 1Jn.4:3; ἤ. ποτέ, now at length, with fut., Rom.1:10 (cf. ἄρτι) \n (AS)","source_line":2380}],"occurrence_count":60,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"já","count":58},{"gloss":"finalmente","count":2}]},"G3":{"id":"G3","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0003","disambiguated_id":"G0003 =","unique_id":"G0003","headword":"Ἀβαδδών","transliteration":"Abaddōn","lexical_morphology":"N:N--T","gloss_en":"Abaddon","definition_en":"Ἀβαδδών (Heb. אֲבַדּוֹן, destruction; LXX, ἀπώλεια, only in Wisdom Lit., of the place of the ruined dead: Job.26:6, 28:22, 31:12, Psa.88:12, Pro.15:11*), indecl.; \n in NT, Abaddon, the angel of the Abyss: Rev.9:11.†\n (AS)","source_line":94}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Abadom","count":1}]},"G3691":{"id":"G3691","source":"