ue_id":"G0431","headword":"ἀνεψιός","transliteration":"anepsios","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"cousin","definition_en":"ἀνεψιός, -οῦ, ὁ\n (cf. Lat. nepos), [in LXX: Num.36:11 ( בֵּן דּוֹד), Tob.7:2 9:6 א * ;] \na cousin: Col.4:10 (MM, VGT, see word).†\n (AS)","source_line":537}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"primo","count":1}]},"G4348":{"id":"G4348","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4348","disambiguated_id":"G4348 =","unique_id":"G4348","headword":"πρόσκομμα","transliteration":"proskomma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"stumbling block","definition_en":"πρόσ-κομμα, -τος, τό\n (προσκόπτω), [in LXX: Exo.23:33 34:12 (מוֹקֵשׁ), Isa.8:14 (נֶגֶף), Jdth.8:22, Sir.17:25, al. ;] \n__(a) a stumble, stumbling: λίθος προσκόμματος (= נֶגֶף אֶבֶן, Isa, l.with), figuratively, Rom.9:32-33, 1Pe.2:8\" (LXX) ; \n __(b) = προσκοπή, an occasion of stumbling, a stumbling-block: metaphorically, Rom.14:13, 20, 1Co.8:9 (Plut.).†\n SYN.: σκάνδαλον (cf. Cremer, 752 f.) (AS)","source_line":4478}],"occurrence_count":6,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tropeço","count":4},{"gloss":"causando-ofensa","count":1},{"gloss":"escândalo","count":1}]},"G48":{"id":"G48","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0048","disambiguated_id":"G0048 =","unique_id":"G0048","headword":"ἁγνίζω","transliteration":"hagnizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to purify","definition_en":"ἁγνίζω (> ἁγνός), \n [in LXX always ceremonially, chiefly for קָדַשׁ ;] \n to purify, cleanse from defilement; \n__(a) ceremonially: Jhn.11:55, Act.21:24, 26 24:18; \n __(b) morally: Jas.4:8, 1Pe.1:22, 1Jn.3:3.\n † SYN.: καθαρίζω, which see (and see: ἁγνός). (AS)","source_line":143}],"occurrence_count":7,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"purificarem","count":1},{"gloss":"contigo","count":1},{"gloss":"tendo-sido-purificado","count":1},{"gloss":"purificado","count":1},{"gloss":"purificai","count":1},{"gloss":"tendo-purificado","count":1},{"gloss":"purifica","