gloss_en":"beyond","definition_en":"ὑπερ-έκεινα \n comp. adv. (see Bl., 28, 2; M, Pr., 99), \n beyond: as prep. with genitive, τὰ ὑ. ὑμῶν, 2Co.10:16 (Byz. and Ecc.1:1-18.).†\n (AS)","source_line":5393}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"pregarmos","count":1}]},"G5412":{"id":"G5412","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5412","disambiguated_id":"G5412 =","unique_id":"G5412","headword":"φορτίζω","transliteration":"phortizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to burden","definition_en":"φορτίζω\n (φόρτος), [in LXX: Eze.16:33 (שָׁחַד) * ;] \nto load: with dupl. accusative, Luk.11:46; pass., to be laden: metaphorically (EV, heavy laden), Mat.11:28.†\n (AS)","source_line":5574}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sobrecarregados","count":1},{"gloss":"carregais","count":1}]},"G5477":{"id":"G5477","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5477","disambiguated_id":"G5477 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H3667A","headword":"Χαναάν","transliteration":"Chanaan","lexical_morphology":"N:N--L","gloss_en":"Canaan","definition_en":"Χαναάν, ἡ indecl. (Heb. כְּנַעַן), \n Canaan: Act.7:11; γῆ Χ., Act.13:19.†\n (AS)","source_line":5643}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Canaã","count":2}]},"G616":{"id":"G616","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0616","disambiguated_id":"G0616 =","unique_id":"G0616","headword":"ἀποκυέω","transliteration":"apokueō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to generate","definition_en":"ἀπο-κυέω\n (Rec. -κύω), -ῶ (ἀπό, κυέω or κύω, to be pregnant), [in LXX: 4Ma.15:17 * ;] \nprop., \"the medical word for birth as the close of pregnancy\" (Hort, Ja., 26 f.). In κοιν, \"an ordinary syn. of τίκτω, but definitely 'perfectivised' (M, Pr., 111 ff.; MM, see word) by the\n ἀπό, and so implying safe delivery,\" to bring forth, give birth to: Jas.1:15, 18.†\n (AS)","source_line":724}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"gera","count":1},{"gloss":"co